    case ' and {v0} map points': return l10n.uid8c8c3da6665(value(0));
    case '1. Create a new project in MapBanai. Open Project Details or Help and copy its project ID (the long UUID).\n2. Create a fresh Google spreadsheet for this project, or open your XLSForm .xlsx in Google Sheets. Keep the exact questionnaire tab names: survey, choices, settings.\n3. Keep the XLSForm header row. Common survey columns: type, name, label, required, relevant, constraint, constraint_message, calculation. Choice columns: list_name, name, label. Settings: form_title, form_id, version.\n4. You do not need to create data tabs or a photo folder. The setup script creates responses, features, photos, revisions and a private Drive photo folder automatically.\n5. Use a fresh spreadsheet and script for each new project. For the recommended single-spreadsheet setup, you do not need to copy spreadsheet IDs.': return l10n.ui54c0efcf9fc5;
    case '1. From your new Google spreadsheet, open Extensions → Apps Script. This connects the script to that spreadsheet; this is what “bound workbook” means.\n2. Copy the complete Code.gs below into the editor. Add two HTML files named Map and Charts, then paste the matching HTML files below.\n3. At the top of Code.gs, replace only PASTE_PROJECT_ID_FROM_MAPBANAI with the project ID you copied. Keep the quotation marks. Leave questionnaireSheetId, dataSheetId, apiKey and photoFolderId at their placeholder values.\n4. Save. Select setupMapBanai in the function dropdown and click Run. Authorize spreadsheet and Drive access with your manager account. It uses this spreadsheet for both questions and collected data, generates a private API key, creates a photo folder and creates the data tabs.\n5. Reload your spreadsheet. Open MapBanai → Connection and setup guide and copy the API key. You can also find MAPBANAI_API_KEY in Apps Script → Project Settings → Script properties. This is a MapBanai password; you do not need Google Cloud API credentials.\n6. In Apps Script, choose Deploy → New deployment → Web app. Set Execute as: Me and Who has access: Anyone. Click Deploy, authorize if asked, and copy the Web app URL ending /exec. Copy the full URL, not the editor address. If Anyone is unavailable, ask your Google Workspace administrator.\n7. In MapBanai Project Details → Cloud Sync, paste the URL and API key. Tap Save, then Test Connection. This verifies the project ID, key and data-sheet access without sending records.\n8. Open Survey Mode → Sync questionnaire → Check Google Sheet → review → Apply update. Collect one test response, sync from Home and check the spreadsheet. Edit the response and sync again to verify revision history.\n9. Export the project with Include sync connection for your trusted field team. Enumerators import it and set My name in the Home three-bar menu. Repeat this fresh setup for each new project.': return l10n.ui0d72badb9fca;
    case 'Acres (ac)': return l10n.ui0daa4f380987;
    case 'Atlas stays at Connecting: this is initialization/loading, not the number of sites. Replace the complete matching Map.html and Code.gs, save, close and reopen the atlas from the spreadsheet menu. Read its visible status/error; check Apps Script → Executions if loading takes more than 45 seconds. The manager map loads pinned Leaflet over HTTPS; internet is required.\n\nInvalid JSON/405: use the deployed /exec web-app URL, not an editor URL or /dev. Check doPost exists and deploy a new script version.\n\nWrong project/key: compare the project ID and key in Code.gs with Project Details; Save the settings in the app.\n\nPermission/setup failure: run setupMapBanai as the owner, check spreadsheet/folder IDs and reserved output-tab headers. Check Apps Script Executions privately for diagnostics.\n\nQuestionnaire errors: verify exact tab/header names, stable form_id and valid XLSForm syntax. Avoid formulas that evaluate differently from the intended XLSForm text; store expressions as plain text.\n\nSlow/busy uploads: completed batches are preserved. Retry Sync to send the remaining records. A server timeout is reported separately from loss of internet. Google service quotas apply; very large deployments need a dedicated server. A record can contain up to 160,000 JSON characters in this supplied backend.\n\nOfficial references: developers.google.com/apps-script/guides/web and developers.google.com/apps-script/reference/spreadsheet/range.': return l10n.uid3d9949c92a8;
    case 'Automatic': return l10n.uiac9041e76816;
    case 'Choose the project and questionnaire, answer the questions, follow required fields and validation messages, then save. Conditional questions follow the XLSForm rules supported by the importer. Review import warnings before fieldwork. Date questions use the date picker. Field quality checks list only saved GPS/photo readings above your selected accuracy review limit. Use Accept accuracy to keep a suitable reading and hide that finding permanently on this device, or View record to inspect it. The limit and decisions are saved per project; Undo restores a just-accepted finding. This does not block photos or alter data. Save drafts to resume incomplete interviews.': return l10n.uie1fb894bb078;
    case 'Edit survey/choices/settings cells in Google Sheets. In the app, select the project → Survey Mode → Sync questionnaire → Check Google Sheet → review → Apply update. New interviews and attribute editors use the new questions. Existing saved records and drafts retain their original form version. Updates require internet; collection remains offline.\n\nOne online XLSForm is served per project by this script; other locally imported forms remain available. Change the displayed label freely, but keep existing question names and form_id stable. Removing/renaming questions can change how historical answers are interpreted. Check warnings and pilot every revised questionnaire before field deployment.': return l10n.ui58167ff8f947;
    case 'Enumerator: collect, correct and sync': return l10n.ui7514aeee4771;
    case 'Feet (ft)': return l10n.ui7d5c63dab944;
    case 'GIS Mode: draw and enter attributes': return l10n.ui9a35340e0499;
    case 'GPS Mode and geotagged photos': return l10n.uid21c6a5da671;
    case 'GPS Mode is independent of projects. It provides location diagnostics and recording. Its compass uses orientation sensors relative to magnetic north, with GPS travel bearing explicitly labelled as a fallback; keep the phone flat and calibrate away from metal when prompted. GNSS altitude is an absolute satellite estimate, not height above your building’s ground floor; indoor reception can give unreliable altitude. Check outdoor reception and vertical accuracy where available.\n\nPhotos require a valid location for geotagging. Accuracy is recorded for review but a strict accuracy threshold does not block taking a photo. Allow location and camera permissions, and give the device time to acquire a location.': return l10n.uibf3148392176;
    case 'Hectares (ha)': return l10n.ui65e00a1aa4fc;
    case 'Import forms, project packages and study maps before leaving connectivity. Prepare offline basemaps where supported; online map tiles need internet. Save field records locally and sync the selected project when connected. Sync sends responses, GIS/study features and photos. Records sync in sequential batches of at most 20. Busy-server responses retry automatically; completed batches remain synced after interruption. Retry sends only remaining records. The supplied backend updates stable record IDs and reuses photo IDs. Saved edits increment response_revision and return to the upload queue. The revisions tab preserves uploaded versions; several offline edits before sync upload only the final version. Deploy the new Code.gs to sync corrections. A conflict stays on the phone for manager review.\n\nManagers: reload the Google spreadsheet → MapBanai → Map workspace or Charts workspace. Maps use the app’s basemaps, designs, independent fonts, category colours and symbols, editable legends and PNG/JPEG downloads. Manager maps accept multiple GeoJSON or shapefile ZIP overlays. Both map and chart workspaces have Fullscreen, with an expanded Sheets dialog when browser fullscreen is blocked. Charts include aggregation, themes and PNG/JPEG/SVG export. These workspaces require an authenticated manager and are not public links.\n\nCollected records are stored as full JSON (including geometry and answers) across json_1 to json_4 output columns. Concatenate those columns to reconstruct a record. The photos tab includes readable metadata, embedded thumbnails and Open photo in Drive links. New uploads add previews automatically. For previously synced photos, reload the spreadsheet and choose MapBanai → Refresh photo previews (up to 50 missing previews per run). Files remain private; the spreadsheet shows embedded thumbnails to its viewers. If a preview cannot be created, use its Drive link. This backend is an upload destination; it does not automatically download other enumerators’ records into your phone.': return l10n.ui2e2fa0ad4e93;
    case 'Kilometers (km)': return l10n.ui6d3be8e36078;
    case 'Manager setup: one workbook or two?': return l10n.uif836181704ed;
    case 'Manager setup: paste and deploy the script': return l10n.uie1ca88d502bf;
    case 'Manager setup: prepare Google Sheets': return l10n.uia120af7937ca;
    case 'Manager: create a project, import its XLSForm, select a questionnaire and add study-area maps. Configure the cloud connection if needed. Export/share the project package with “Include sync connection” selected for trusted enumerators.\n\nEnumerator: Home → three-bar menu → My name. Import the project package and select it. Survey Mode → Sync questionnaire checks for updated questions. Collect offline in Survey Mode, GIS Mode or Visit a study site. Home → three-bar menu → My responses lets you review and edit saved responses. Home → Cloud Sync uploads new records and corrections when connected. Each correction keeps the original collector and stable ID, records the editor and advances the response revision; it is separate from questionnaire version. The same project and questions are used in GIS and Study Area modes. GPS Mode works independently.': return l10n.ui8762dae21dde;
    case 'Meters (m)': return l10n.uiaf34806a7287;
    case 'Miles (mi)': return l10n.uib0b04ac9caed;
    case 'Offline work, cloud sync and photos': return l10n.ui682761a623ce;
    case 'Open Project Details → Reusable templates. Save the whole project or its selected layer and questionnaire. From Project Setup → Reusable templates, create a new project from a saved template. Project Details also lets you add template layers to the current project. Templates preserve forms, layer names and setup; they exclude site geometry, visits, photos and cloud keys. New projects and added layers receive fresh identities. Configure the new project’s cloud connection separately. Templates are local and included in database backups. To share with another phone, create a project from the template and export its project package.': return l10n.uia71aaef663f0;
    case 'Open WebMap for the selected project. Use Explore → Colours & categories: choose any text/numeric answer column (such as layer), then Categories for per-value colours and visibility or Graduated for numeric colours. Geometry type is the uniform default. Edit category names, colours and symbols in Download Map. Filter and inspect features, choose a map theme, turn labels on/off, and compose a poster or map-only image with a title and subtitle. Export PNG for clear graphics or JPEG for smaller files. Tap the separate Download Map button to open 12 designs, custom colours, portrait/landscape, aspect ratio and pixel resolution (HD, Full HD, QHD, 4K or custom). Download PNG/JPEG opens the phone file picker; Share PNG/JPEG opens sharing. Basemap tiles must be loaded and exportable; offline/data-only exports may lack the basemap. Rename mapped legend categories, choose point symbols/line patterns/polygon outlines or upload PNG/self-contained SVG icons (up to 512 KB and 2048 pixels per side). Title, subtitle and legend fonts can be chosen independently, with four bundled offline fonts. Text, symbols and north arrow scale with image resolution; choose Standard/Large/Extra large for readability. The map covers over 80% of the exported poster, with a compact title and legend below. Map extent defaults to Fit visible data; choose Current map view to preserve your framing. Coordinates below the title are omitted. Only included basemaps receive attribution; record counts and no-basemap notices are omitted.': return l10n.ui78f2a306509a;
    case 'Open a study-area feature → Site timeline / add observation, or select a feature in the guided visit screen → Site timeline. Choose Add observation / start visit to record another measurement. Finish each visit separately; earlier answers remain linked to the same stable feature UUID. Choose a questionnaire and numeric question (such as salinity) to compare visits. Keep question names and units consistent. Export all observations as CSV; feature_uuid joins them to study-map GeoJSON. Imported visit history is included and deduplicated with local interviews. Timelines show locally available history; cloud sync does not download other devices’ visits.': return l10n.ui0f3c63f41614;
    case 'Project packages share project definitions, forms and study-layer configuration; they are not a backup of responses or photos. “Include sync connection” is optional and includes the URL and key. Preserve the same project identity across the team; duplicating a project creates a different identity that needs its own backend configuration.\n\nUse the app backup/export tools for collected data and keep copies outside the phone. Installing an update over the existing signed app preserves local storage; uninstalling or clearing app storage removes local information. Save cloud connection settings before exporting a package.': return l10n.ui4452be7b875c;
    case 'Recommended: one Google workbook + one Apps Script web app + one private API key per project. Keep questionnaire tabs (survey, choices, settings) and output tabs (responses, features, photos, revisions) in the same workbook. No second URL or key is needed.\n\nFor separate storage, use two workbooks: questionnaireSheetId points to the XLSForm workbook; dataSheetId points to the collected-data workbook. The same script handles both, so the app still uses one URL and key. Two independent deployments/keys are not configured in this version.\n\nUse a separate setup for each project. Keep questionnaire editing with managers; enumerators only need the MapBanai project package. API keys give access to the project endpoint; share packages containing them only with your field team.': return l10n.ui48f8d1dd5266;
    case 'Reference vector layers and backgrounds': return l10n.uifd76b27cda7d;
    case 'Repeated observations and site timelines': return l10n.ui12432a3ccda1;
    case 'Reusable project and layer templates': return l10n.ui6cb726ab7ebc;
    case 'Select the project and one of its study-area maps. Import from the top toolbar; GeoJSON and GeoPackage can be selected regardless of Android MIME filtering. ZIP shapefile companions together for attributes. Files opened externally offer an existing project, new project or view-only preview. Add new Layer is inside the study-layer selector; the plus button opens the questionnaire at a fresh GPS position. Edit feature requires a questionnaire for new/Updated features; other statuses have an optional Fill questionnaire checkbox. Skipping keeps previous answers. Categories & colors includes Verification status coloring and starts with a single color and lets you explicitly choose a column, category colors/visibility and point size.  Use separate named maps for salinity rounds, household verification or the full study area. Start/resume a field visit for that selected area. Verify existing sites, record new information or update attributes using the selected questionnaire. Visit history preserves the review trail. Assign old unassigned sites to a project explicitly. Export the updated area after fieldwork.': return l10n.ui1a25286391c7;
    case 'Select the project, layer and survey. Add a point, line or polygon, then enter information using the selected survey questions. Existing geometry can be edited and its attributes updated. Define questions in the selected survey form; the separate Project Settings field editor has been removed, while old field values remain stored. Use consistent identifiers to connect a feature with a site or repeat visit. Export spatial data when you need analysis in GIS software.': return l10n.ui3ba9b97177d2;
    case 'Sharing, backups and app updates': return l10n.uicba2a97abd4c;
    case 'Square feet (ft²)': return l10n.ui1cc6418b3dc4;
